      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nFollow-up to #60532. On SM90 an NVFP4 KV cache already decodes with FlashInfer's fa2 tensor-core decode, because XQA reads NVFP4 only on SM12x. #60532 sends uniform spec-decode queries through that decode only below SM90, so SM90 with NVFP4 still splits verification steps off as prefills and reports `UNIFORM_SINGLE_TOKEN_DECODE`. This applies the same fa2 path there.\n\n## Claims\n\n- With an NVFP4 KV cache on SM90, FlashInfer spec decode runs its verification steps in full CUDA graphs. With Qwen3.8-27B NVFP4 and MTP (3 tokens), decode goes from 97.3 to 130.4 tok/s at TP=1.\n- Other KV cache dtypes on SM90, and every other architecture, keep their decode selection and graph support.\n\n## Validation\n\n`test_flashinfer_nvfp4_decode_correctness` now also runs on SM90. It decodes single-token and 4-token queries over an NVFP4 cache, eager and under CUDA graph replay, against the fa2 prefill that wrote the cache, and checks that 4-token queries are planned with `q_len_per_req=4`.\n\nOn SM80, where nothing changes, with the FlashInfer 0.7.2 release wheel that vLLM pins: `pytest tests/v1/attention/test_attention_backends.py tests/v1/attention/test_flashinfer_dcp_spec_reorder.py -k \"flashinfer or FLASHINFER\"` gives 35 passed, 5 skipped.\n\nOn SM90, Qwen3.8-27B NVFP4 weights, NVFP4 KV cache, TP=1, batch 1, MTP with 3 tokens: 97.3 tok/s on `main` (`PIECEWISE`) and 130.4 tok/s with this PR (decode `FULL`).\n\n## Details\n\n- `_use_fa2_native_decode()` takes the cache's NVFP4 flag and is true on SM90 when the cache is NVFP4. The builder passes `is_kvcache_nvfp4`, so `supports_spec_as_decode` and the explicit `backend=\"fa2\"` decode wrapper from #60532 follow.\n- `get_cudagraph_support` takes the fa2 branch when every attention spec decodes with fa2. Otherwise the existing XQA checks apply unchanged, and they already report `UNIFORM_SINGLE_TOKEN_DECODE` for an NVFP4 spec on SM90.\n- `get_varlen_cudagraph_max_query_len` is unchanged: on SM90 the decode kernel is XQA, never trtllm-gen, so the bound is already `None`.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
